BandC wrote:
>
> Is there such thing as "wasting" a skill point (like a constant number
> of skill points you can ever obtain)?

Absolutely.  Skill slots are a very limited resource and the
number of weapon classes and spell schools each character
class is able to enhance far exceeds that total.  Is is
actually a trap on the part of the DevTeam to tempt
inexperienced players to enhance the wrong stuff and then
die later in the game as a result of insufficient skill.

> Or "wasting" is meant in terms of
> time lost using a certain item?

Absolutely.  If an item is a dead end in the long term then
spending time on it wastes moves.  Given the choice between
using an item that does give long term benefit in addition
to short term benefit, or an item that gives short term
benefit and negative long term impact, which should you
use?

> Should I refrain spending skill points
> for things I don't wanna develop for long term?

Take the 29 possible slots and work out where you will end
up if you use them with strategy in mind.  Then take them
and work out where you will end up if you enhance every
time it is offered.

This isn't to say you should refuse to kill any monster
with your whip if a nymph has stolen your pick.  Use what
you have to be sure.  Select wisely among what you do
have and select strategically what you advance.


